# FundLens Frontend README

## Purpose

This document is the detailed implementation specification for the FundLens frontend.

The frontend has one core job:

> **Filter and explain financial information according to what the user actually needs, without reducing access to information they explicitly request.**

There are two presentation modes:

- **Beginner:** instinctive, visual, low cognitive load, progressive disclosure.
- **Advanced:** analytical, configurable, dense where useful.

They are two views of the **same underlying financial intelligence**.

---

# 1. Product Architecture

```text
                         USER
                           |
              +------------+------------+
              |                         |
              v                         v
       PERSONALIZED HOME             SEARCH
       "Help me decide"        "I know what I want"
              |                         |
       recommendations          requested scheme
       + user context                    |
              |                         |
              +------------+------------+
                           |
                           v
                      FUND DETAIL
                           |
                  +--------+--------+
                  |                 |
                  v                 v
              BEGINNER          ADVANCED
                  |                 |
                  +--------+--------+
                           |
                           v
                    SAME ANALYTICS
```

### Core principle

**Search determines WHAT fund the user wants.**

**Personalization determines HOW that fund is presented.**

If a user explicitly searches for a scheme, FundLens must not hide it because another fund scores better for their profile.

