# 11. Search & Direct Fund Access

Search is a first-class product entry point.

Two user intents:

```text
"Help me decide"
        ↓
Personalized Home

"I know what I want"
        ↓
Search
```

Search must not be filtered by personalization.

## Search bar

```text
┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 🔍 Search mutual funds               │
│                                      │
│ Search by fund, AMC, category...     │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Users should be able to search by:

- Scheme name.
- AMC.
- Category.
- Fund family.
- ISIN / scheme identifier later.

## Search results

Typing:

```text
parag
```

could produce:

```text
Parag Parikh Flexi Cap
Parag Parikh ELSS Tax Saver
Parag Parikh Dynamic Asset Allocation
```

Result card:

```text
┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Parag Parikh Flexi Cap               │
│ Flexi Cap • Direct • Growth          │
│ PPFAS Mutual Fund                    │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Search ranking

Search ranking follows search relevance.

```text
User query
   ↓
Search engine
   ↓
Relevant schemes
   ↓
Selected scheme
   ↓
Personalized presentation
```

Do not do:

```text
User query
   ↓
Personalization filter
   ↓
Hide schemes
```

## Search API

Conceptually:

```http
GET /funds/search?q=parag
```

Example:

```json
{
  "query": "parag",
  "results": [
    {
      "scheme_id": "12345",
      "scheme_name": "Parag Parikh Flexi Cap Fund",
      "amc": "PPFAS Mutual Fund",
      "category": "Flexi Cap",
      "plan": "Direct",
      "option": "Growth"
    }
  ]
}
```

Use the existing backend contract if it differs.

## Search states

- [ ] Empty.
- [ ] Loading.
- [ ] Results.
- [ ] No results.
- [ ] Network error.

Never show fabricated `0%` or placeholder financial results as real data.

