# 15. Beginner Visual Language

Every major metric follows:

```text
VISUAL SIGNAL
      ↓
PLAIN LANGUAGE
      ↓
KEY NUMBER
      ↓
DETAIL ON DEMAND
```

Example:

```text
HOW MUCH CAN IT FALL?

●●●●●●○○○○

Moderate

Worst historical fall
-18.4%

[ Why does this matter? ]
```

Tap "Why":

```text
Maximum drawdown: -18.4%

This measures the largest peak-to-trough
fall in the fund's history.

[ See evidence ]
```

Advanced can show the complete metric definition and dates.

---

# 16. Beginner Gamification Rules

Borrow interaction mechanics from products such as Duolingo, not their childish personality.

Use:

- [ ] Progress indicators.
- [ ] Clear visual states.
- [ ] Immediate selection feedback.
- [ ] Small transitions.
- [ ] One clear next action.
- [ ] Progressive disclosure.
- [ ] Visual comparison.
- [ ] Completion feedback.

Avoid:

- [ ] Coins.
- [ ] Fake points.
- [ ] Investing streaks.
- [ ] Confetti for financial decisions.
- [ ] Competitive leaderboards.
- [ ] Countdown pressure.
- [ ] Childish mascots everywhere.

Money is not a game.

